IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-core`
IMPORT `aia-timeline`
IMPORT `aia-literacy`

-- Tests of aia-literacy.l4 (Article 4, as enacted and as replaced by the Omnibus). Expected values are written by hand from the text.
-- 1 February 2025 is the day before Chapter I applies; 2 February 2025 is the first day. 26 July 2026 is under the text as enacted, 27 July 2026 under the text as amended.

§ `Chapter I begins to apply on 2 February 2025`

#ASSERT NOT (`Art 4 Chapter I has begun to apply on the date asked` (Date 1 2 2025))
#ASSERT `Art 4 Chapter I has begun to apply on the date asked` (Date 2 2 2025)
#ASSERT `Art 4 Chapter I has begun to apply on the date asked` (Date 27 7 2026)

§ `Article 4(1): who owes the duty (the same addressees in both texts)`

-- args: date, provider, deployer
#ASSERT `Art 4(1) the party owes the duty to take measures regarding AI literacy` (Date 1 2 2025) TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 4(1) the party owes the duty to take measures regarding AI literacy` (Date 2 2 2025) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 4(1) the party owes the duty to take measures regarding AI literacy` (Date 2 2 2025) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 4(1) the party owes the duty to take measures regarding AI literacy` (Date 26 7 2026) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 4(1) the party owes the duty to take measures regarding AI literacy` (Date 27 7 2026) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): neither a provider nor a deployer.
#ASSERT `Art 4(1) the party owes the duty to take measures regarding AI literacy` (Date 2 2 2025) FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 4(1) the party owes the duty to take measures regarding AI literacy` (Date 27 7 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Article 4(1): the measures; the two texts name different aims, so a case on each side of 27 July 2026`

-- args: date, concern literacy of staff and others, take into account knowledge and context, consider the persons on whom systems are used, aim: ensure a sufficient level, aim: support the development
-- Before Chapter I applies: NOTHING.
#ASSERT `Art 4(1) the measures meet the duty to take measures regarding AI literacy` (Date 1 2 2025) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- As enacted (the aim is "to ensure, to their best extent, a sufficient level of AI literacy"):
#ASSERT `Art 4(1) the measures meet the duty to take measures regarding AI literacy` (Date 2 2 2025) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 4(1) the measures meet the duty to take measures regarding AI literacy` (Date 26 7 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 4(1) the measures meet the duty to take measures regarding AI literacy` (Date 26 7 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- As amended (the aim is "to support the development of AI literacy"):
#ASSERT `Art 4(1) the measures meet the duty to take measures regarding AI literacy` (Date 27 7 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 4(1) the measures meet the duty to take measures regarding AI literacy` (Date 27 7 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Each element missing, in each text: FALSE-kind (a bare "shall" not done; fork F-4-1).
#ASSERT `Art 4(1) the measures meet the duty to take measures regarding AI literacy` (Date 26 7 2026) FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 4(1) the measures meet the duty to take measures regarding AI literacy` (Date 26 7 2026) TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 4(1) the measures meet the duty to take measures regarding AI literacy` (Date 26 7 2026) TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 4(1) the measures meet the duty to take measures regarding AI literacy` (Date 27 7 2026) FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 4(1) the measures meet the duty to take measures regarding AI literacy` (Date 27 7 2026) TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 4(1) the measures meet the duty to take measures regarding AI literacy` (Date 27 7 2026) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Article 4(1), last sentence: no specific level need be guaranteed (as amended only)`

-- args: date, provider, deployer
#ASSERT `Art 4(1) the party must guarantee a specific level of AI literacy of an individual` (Date 26 7 2026) TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 4(1) the party must guarantee a specific level of AI literacy of an individual` (Date 27 7 2026) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 4(1) the party must guarantee a specific level of AI literacy of an individual` (Date 27 7 2026) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 4(1) the party must guarantee a specific level of AI literacy of an individual` (Date 27 7 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 4(1) the party must guarantee a specific level of AI literacy of an individual` (Date 1 2 2025) TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Article 4(2) and (3): as amended only`

#ASSERT `Art 4(2) the Commission and the Member States must support and facilitate the efforts of the party to fulfil the obligation under paragraph 1` (Date 26 7 2026) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 4(2) the Commission and the Member States must support and facilitate the efforts of the party to fulfil the obligation under paragraph 1` (Date 27 7 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 4(2) the Commission and the Member States must support and facilitate the efforts of the party to fulfil the obligation under paragraph 1` (Date 27 7 2026) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 4(2) the Commission must publish practical examples of how to comply with the obligation under paragraph 1` (Date 26 7 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 4(2) the Commission must publish practical examples of how to comply with the obligation under paragraph 1` (Date 27 7 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 4(3) the Board must adopt recommendations to support the promotion of AI literacy` (Date 26 7 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 4(3) the Board must adopt recommendations to support the promotion of AI literacy` (Date 27 7 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 4(3) the Board must adopt recommendations to support the promotion of AI literacy` (Date 1 2 2025) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `The regulative rule: a provider and a deployer each owe the measures (no time limit, no consequence, so no breach path)`

-- The rule is a MUST with no WITHIN and no LEST: a trace in which the party acts reads FULFILLED, and no trace reaches BREACH. See NOTES.md, Rules with no breach path.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 4(1) the provider's duty to take measures regarding AI literacy` (Date 2 2 2025) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Provider DOES `Art 4(1) take measures regarding AI literacy` AT 5
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 4(1) the provider's duty to take measures regarding AI literacy` (Date 27 7 2026) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Provider DOES `Art 4(1) take measures regarding AI literacy` AT 400
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 4(1) the deployer's duty to take measures regarding AI literacy` (Date 27 7 2026) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Deployer DOES `Art 4(1) take measures regarding AI literacy` AT 5
-- Before Chapter I applies nothing is owed.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 4(1) the deployer's duty to take measures regarding AI literacy` (Date 1 2 2025) AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 1000
